invariant: INV-43
file: p256_wide_verify_point.c
catches: p256_verify_equiv_test
reason: the host verifier's mixed addition doubles the running sum where
  the entry of the table of multiples of G it adds is the sum's negative,
  whose sum is the point at infinity. The case of
  bin/p256_verify_equiv_test under the key -G/2 with u1 = 1 and u2 = 2
  brings the running sum to -G just before G is added, and wants the pair
  refused.

--- old
    p256_wide_fe_sub(&rr, &s2, &a->y);
    if (fe_is_zero(&h)) {
        if (fe_is_zero(&rr)) {
            point_double(o, a);
        } else {
            memset(o, 0, sizeof *o);
        }
--- new
    p256_wide_fe_sub(&rr, &s2, &a->y);
    if (fe_is_zero(&h)) {
        point_double(o, a);
